{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A component version of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMatchRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" hook. It accepts the same options as the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMatchRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" with additional props to aid in conditional rendering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"matchroute-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MatchRoute props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MatchRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the same options as the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMatchRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" hook with additional props to aid in conditional rendering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"props-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"...props"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"link","href":"./UseMatchRouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseMatchRouteOptions"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"children-prop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.ReactNode"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component that will be rendered if the route is matched."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"((params: TParams | false) => React.ReactNode)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that will be called with the matched route's params or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" if no route was matched. This can be useful for components that need to always render, but render different props based on a route match or not."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"matchroute-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MatchRoute returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Either the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" prop or the return value of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { MatchRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <MatchRoute to=\"/posts/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }} pending>\n        {(match) => <Spinner show={!!match} wait=\"delay-50\" />}\n      </MatchRoute>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"matchroute-props","text":"MatchRoute props","level":2},{"id":"props-prop","text":"...props prop","level":3},{"id":"children-prop","text":"children prop","level":3},{"id":"matchroute-returns","text":"MatchRoute returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA component version of the `useMatchRoute` hook. It accepts the same options as the `useMatchRoute` with additional props to aid in conditional rendering.\n\n## MatchRoute props\n\nThe `MatchRoute` component accepts the same options as the `useMatchRoute` hook with additional props to aid in conditional rendering.\n\n### `...props` prop\n\n- Type: [`UseMatchRouteOptions`](./UseMatchRouteOptionsType.md)\n\n### `children` prop\n\n- Optional\n- `React.ReactNode`\n  - The component that will be rendered if the route is matched.\n- `((params: TParams | false) => React.ReactNode)`\n  - A function that will be called with the matched route's params or `false` if no route was matched. This can be useful for components that need to always render, but render different props based on a route match or not.\n\n## MatchRoute returns\n\nEither the `children` prop or the return value of the `children` function.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { MatchRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <MatchRoute to=\"/posts/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }} pending>\n        {(match) => <Spinner show={!!match} wait=\"delay-50\" />}\n      </MatchRoute>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: matchRouteComponent\ntitle: MatchRoute component\n---\n\nA component version of the `useMatchRoute` hook. It accepts the same options as the `useMatchRoute` with additional props to aid in conditional rendering.\n\n## MatchRoute props\n\nThe `MatchRoute` component accepts the same options as the `useMatchRoute` hook with additional props to aid in conditional rendering.\n\n### `...props` prop\n\n- Type: [`UseMatchRouteOptions`](./UseMatchRouteOptionsType.md)\n\n### `children` prop\n\n- Optional\n- `React.ReactNode`\n  - The component that will be rendered if the route is matched.\n- `((params: TParams | false) => React.ReactNode)`\n  - A function that will be called with the matched route's params or `false` if no route was matched. This can be useful for components that need to always render, but render different props based on a route match or not.\n\n## MatchRoute returns\n\nEither the `children` prop or the return value of the `children` function.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { MatchRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <MatchRoute to=\"/posts/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }} pending>\n        {(match) => <Spinner show={!!match} wait=\"delay-50\" />}\n      </MatchRoute>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
